-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hydbring</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Cvek</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cardiovascular and fluid regulatory mechanisms during pregnancy and lactation in small ruminants</article-title><source>Trends Comp Biochem Physiol</source><year>1998</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>283</fpage><lpage>296</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Peeters</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Grutters</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>CB</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Distribution of cardiac output in the unstressed guinea pig</article-title><source>Am J Obstet Gynecol</source><year>1980</year><volume>138</volume><fpage>1177</fpage><lpage>1184</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7446627</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scantlebury</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Butterwick</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Speakman</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Energetics of lactation in domestic dog (Canis familiaris) breeds of two sizes</article-title><source>Comp Biochem Physiol Part A</source><year>2000</year><volume>125</volume><fpage>197</fpage><lpage>210</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1095-6433(99)00175-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>SAS</surname><given-names>Institute</given-names></name></person-group><source>User's Guide: Statistics, version 6.12</source><year>1996</year><publisher-name>SAS Institute Inc, Cary, NC, USA</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-t